var SXPI={g4:'Read the passage and answer the questions. (Passage written for this set.)\n\nFor almost a year, Meera had not opened the battered old piano in the corner of the drawing room. Her teacher, Mr Fernandes, had moved to Goa, and with him had gone the Thursday lessons, the sharp tap of his pencil on the music stand, and her belief that she could ever play well. The silence had settled like dust over the keys.\n\nThen her little cousin Arjun came to stay for the holidays. On the second evening, Meera heard a sound she had almost forgotten: a few notes, clumsy and uneven, but unmistakably a tune. Arjun was standing on tiptoe, picking out a nursery rhyme with one finger.\n\n“Can you play it properly?” he asked. Meera was reluctant. She told him she had forgotten everything. But he looked at her with such certainty that she sat down. She placed her hands on the keys, and to her surprise her fingers remembered what her mind had forgotten. The first piece Mr Fernandes had taught her came back, slowly at first, then with something like joy.\n\nThat night she wrote to her teacher for the first time in months.'};

